---
import '../design/design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from '../design/SketchSheet.astro';
import SketchArrow from '../design/SketchArrow.astro';
const { headingLevel = 3 } = Astro.props;
// The old h4 (level 4 title, level 3 panel label) took its look from the sketch-sheet styles.
const titleClass = headingLevel === 4 ? 'aid-title panel-title' : 'aid-title';
const subtitleClass = headingLevel === 4 ? 'aid-panel-title' : 'aid-panel-title panel-title';
---
<figure id="isolation-write-skew" class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface" aria-labelledby="write-skew-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · Repeatable Read</span>
  <p class={titleClass} id="write-skew-title">Concurrent changes to the featured display</p>
  <p>The featured display has P7 and P8 enabled. A staff transaction may hide one product only if the other stays enabled. The two transactions overlap and change different rows.</p>
  <div class="skew-start"><SketchSheet><p class={subtitleClass}>Initial committed display</p><div class="skew-values"><span>P7: enabled</span><span>P8: enabled</span></div></SketchSheet></div>
  <div class="skew-fork"><SketchArrow direction="down" /><span>Each transaction reads this view</span><SketchArrow direction="down" /></div>
  <div class="skew-decisions">
    <SketchSheet tone="blue"><p class={subtitleClass}>Staff A</p><p>Reads <strong>P8: enabled</strong></p><p>Decision: hide P7</p><hr /><p>Writes <strong>P7: disabled</strong></p><small>Does not write P8</small></SketchSheet>
    <SketchSheet tone="blue"><p class={subtitleClass}>Staff B</p><p>Reads <strong>P7: enabled</strong></p><p>Decision: hide P8</p><hr /><p>Writes <strong>P8: disabled</strong></p><small>Does not write P7</small></SketchSheet>
  </div>
  <div class="skew-fork"><SketchArrow direction="down" /><span>Both commit in this Repeatable Read schedule</span><SketchArrow direction="down" /></div>
  <SketchSheet tone="amber"><p class={subtitleClass}>Combined committed result</p><div class="skew-values"><span>P7: <strong>disabled</strong></span><span>P8: <strong>disabled</strong></span></div><p>The display is empty. No transaction overwrote the other’s row.</p></SketchSheet>
  <figcaption>The stable views preserved both reads; they did not coordinate the decisions. If A ran completely before B, B would see P7 disabled and leave P8 enabled. The opposite order would leave P7 enabled. Both products disabled matches neither serial order. PostgreSQL Serializable prevents both transactions from committing this outcome by rejecting one; it does not choose a preferred product.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .aid-title { margin:0 0 .7rem; font:500 1.4rem/1.35 var(--font-serif); }
  .aid-panel-title { margin:0 0 .65rem; font:600 .875rem/1.4 var(--font-sans); }
  .skew-start { max-width:26rem; margin:1.2rem auto 0; }
  .skew-values { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.6rem 1.2rem; }
  .skew-fork { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-around; gap:.5rem; margin:.5rem 0; }
  .skew-fork > span { text-align:center; max-width:19rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.8125rem; }
  .skew-decisions { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1rem; }
  hr { border:0; border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule); margin:.8rem 0; }
  small { display:block; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  @media(max-width:440px) { .skew-decisions { gap:.4rem; } .skew-decisions p:not(.aid-panel-title) { font-size:.8rem; } .skew-fork > span { font-size:.75rem; } }
</style>
